# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "1. Recap of the spinless 1D Fermi-Hubbard system {#1-recap-of-the-spinless-1d-fermi-hubbard-system}"
msgstr "1. Imbasan semula sistem Fermi-Hubbard 1D tanpa spin {#1-recap-of-the-spinless-1d-fermi-hubbard-system}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The 1D guide writes the model with **vertex** and **transfer** operators,\n"
"$V_j = 1 - 2a_j^\\dagger a_j$ and $T_{jk} = -\\tfrac12 (a_j^\\dagger - a_j)(a_k^\\dagger + a_k)$. With these operators,\n"
"hopping is $t\\,(T_{j,j+1} + T_{j+1,j})$, and the density-density interaction is a product of $V$ operators.\n"
msgstr ""
"Panduan 1D menulis model dengan operator **bucu** dan **pindahan**,\n"
"$V_j = 1 - 2a_j^\\dagger a_j$ dan $T_{jk} = -\\tfrac12 (a_j^\\dagger - a_j)(a_k^\\dagger + a_k)$. Dengan operator ini,\n"
"lompatan ialah $t\\,(T_{j,j+1} + T_{j+1,j})$, dan interaksi ketumpatan-ketumpatan ialah hasil darab operator $V$.\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/spinful-fermi-hubbard-dynamics/extracted-outputs/0b9ab5a2-0.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/spinful-fermi-hubbard-dynamics/extracted-outputs/0b9ab5a2-0.avif)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This tutorial reuses three main ideas from that guide:\n"
msgstr "Tutorial ini menggunakan semula tiga idea utama daripada panduan itu:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Group terms before you map them.** Transfer operators along a directed path commute, and form a *flow set*. On a chain, the flow sets are the\n"
"east-pointing arrows (dark orange), the west-pointing arrows (light orange), and the diagonal interaction terms. The\n"
"drawing shows the arrows of the spinless chain between its sites. Spinless sites are blue in every drawing.\n"
msgstr ""
"**Kumpulkan sebutan sebelum anda memetakannya.** Operator pindahan di sepanjang laluan berarah saling kalis tukar, dan membentuk *set aliran*. Pada rantai, set aliran ialah\n"
"anak panah menghala ke timur (jingga tua), anak panah menghala ke barat (jingga muda), dan sebutan interaksi pepenjuru. Lukisan\n"
"menunjukkan anak panah rantai tanpa spin antara tapaknya. Tapak tanpa spin berwarna biru dalam setiap lukisan.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Use an ancilla qubit to gain structure.** The parity-delocalized fermion-to-qubit encoding stores cumulative parities.\n"
"One extra qubit (an ancilla, which is green in every drawing) turns a whole flow set into weight-1 Pauli operators.\n"
msgstr ""
"**Gunakan qubit ancilla untuk mendapatkan struktur.** Pengekodan fermion-ke-qubit terdelokalisasi-pariti menyimpan pariti longgokan.\n"
"Satu qubit tambahan (ancilla, yang berwarna hijau dalam setiap lukisan) menukar keseluruhan set aliran kepada operator Pauli berat-1.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Use the structure to synthesize circuits.** A single Clifford circuit diagonalizes a whole flow set, so the circuit depth does not\n"
"grow with the chain length.\n"
msgstr ""
"**Gunakan struktur untuk mensintesis circuit.** Satu circuit Clifford mendiagonalkan keseluruhan set aliran, jadi kedalaman circuit tidak\n"
"bertambah dengan panjang rantai.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "2. Spin: blocked or interleaved mode ordering {#2-spin-blocked-or-interleaved-mode-ordering}"
msgstr "2. Spin: susunan mod berblok atau berselang-seli {#2-spin-blocked-or-interleaved-mode-ordering}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This tutorial uses the spinful Fermi-Hubbard model. On a 1D chain of sites, its Hamiltonian is as follows:\n"
msgstr "Tutorial ini menggunakan model Fermi-Hubbard berspin. Pada rantai 1D tapak, Hamiltoniannya adalah seperti berikut:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"H = -t \\sum_{j,\\sigma} \\left(a_{j\\sigma}^\\dagger a_{j+1,\\sigma} + \\text{h.c.}\\right) +\n"
"\\frac{U}{2} \\sum_j \\left(n_{j\\uparrow} - \\tfrac12\\right)\\left(n_{j\\downarrow} - \\tfrac12\\right)\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"H = -t \\sum_{j,\\sigma} \\left(a_{j\\sigma}^\\dagger a_{j+1,\\sigma} + \\text{h.c.}\\right) +\n"
"\\frac{U}{2} \\sum_j \\left(n_{j\\uparrow} - \\tfrac12\\right)\\left(n_{j\\downarrow} - \\tfrac12\\right)\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The vertex and transfer operators do not represent spin. They see $2L$ fermionic modes, so you decide which mode index\n"
"belongs to which (site, spin) pair. Two orderings are natural: **blocked** (all spin-up modes first, then all spin-down\n"
"modes) and **interleaved** (the spin-up and spin-down modes of a site next to each other). Both orderings describe the same physics, but they\n"
"couple different modes, and the encoding and the hardware see those couplings.\n"
msgstr ""
"Operator bucu dan pindahan tidak mewakili spin. Mereka melihat $2L$ mod fermion, jadi anda yang menentukan indeks mod yang\n"
"milik pasangan (tapak, spin) yang mana. Dua susunan adalah semula jadi: **berblok** (semua mod spin-atas dahulu, kemudian semua mod spin-bawah)\n"
"dan **berselang-seli** (mod spin-atas dan spin-bawah bagi sesuatu tapak bersebelahan). Kedua-dua susunan menerangkan fizik yang sama, tetapi\n"
"menggandingkan mod yang berbeza, dan pengekodan serta perkakasan melihat gandingan tersebut.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The choice of ordering changes the distance that the hopping terms and the on-site interaction terms must cover:\n"
msgstr "Pilihan susunan mengubah jarak yang mesti dilitupi oleh sebutan lompatan dan sebutan interaksi dalam-tapak:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Ordering | Spin-up site $j$ | Spin-down site $j$ | Modes that a hop connects | Modes that the on-site term connects |\n"
"|---|---|---|---|---|\n"
"| **Blocked** | $j$ | $L + j$ | $j \\leftrightarrow j+1$ | $j \\leftrightarrow L + j$ |\n"
"| **Interleaved** | $2j$ | $2j + 1$ | $2j \\leftrightarrow 2j+2$ | $2j \\leftrightarrow 2j+1$ |\n"
msgstr ""
"| Susunan | Tapak $j$ spin-atas | Tapak $j$ spin-bawah | Mod yang disambungkan oleh lompatan | Mod yang disambungkan oleh sebutan dalam-tapak |\n"
"|---|---|---|---|---|\n"
"| **Berblok** | $j$ | $L + j$ | $j \\leftrightarrow j+1$ | $j \\leftrightarrow L + j$ |\n"
"| **Berselang-seli** | $2j$ | $2j + 1$ | $2j \\leftrightarrow 2j+2$ | $2j \\leftrightarrow 2j+1$ |\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The following drawing shows both orderings for $L = 4$ sites. Each node is a mode ($V_m$, as in section 1) at the horizontal\n"
"position of its mode index. The spin-up modes are on the top chain (dark blue), and the spin-down modes are on the bottom chain\n"
"(light blue). The arrows along a chain are the hops. East-pointing hops are dark orange and west-pointing hops are light orange, as in\n"
"the flow sets of section 1. The dotted blue link between the two modes of a site is the on-site interaction, and the grid\n"
"marks the position of every mode on the line.\n"
msgstr ""
"Lukisan berikut menunjukkan kedua-dua susunan untuk $L = 4$ tapak. Setiap nod ialah mod ($V_m$, seperti dalam bahagian 1) pada kedudukan\n"
"mendatar indeks modnya. Mod spin-atas berada pada rantai atas (biru tua), dan mod spin-bawah berada pada rantai bawah\n"
"(biru muda). Anak panah di sepanjang rantai ialah lompatan. Lompatan menghala ke timur berwarna jingga tua dan lompatan menghala ke barat berwarna jingga muda, seperti dalam\n"
"set aliran bahagian 1. Pautan biru bertitik antara dua mod sesuatu tapak ialah interaksi dalam-tapak, dan grid\n"
"menandakan kedudukan setiap mod pada garisan.\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/spinful-fermi-hubbard-dynamics/extracted-outputs/c353bde8-0.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/spinful-fermi-hubbard-dynamics/extracted-outputs/c353bde8-0.avif)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The ordering is visible in the on-site links. In blocked order, the on-site links are long, because the on-site term couples mode $j$ and\n"
"mode $L + j$, while the hops stay between neighboring modes. In interleaved order, the on-site links are short (mode $2j$ to mode\n"
"$2j + 1$), but the hops skip over the mode of the other spin. In both orderings, every term still acts on **two modes**.\n"
msgstr ""
"Susunan ini kelihatan pada pautan dalam-tapak. Dalam susunan berblok, pautan dalam-tapak panjang, kerana sebutan dalam-tapak menggandingkan mod $j$ dan\n"
"mod $L + j$, manakala lompatan kekal antara mod berjiran. Dalam susunan berselang-seli, pautan dalam-tapak pendek (mod $2j$ ke mod\n"
"$2j + 1$), tetapi lompatan melangkau mod bagi spin yang lain. Dalam kedua-dua susunan, setiap sebutan tetap bertindak pada **dua mod**.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"If $m(j, \\sigma)$ is the mode of site $j$ and spin $\\sigma$, hopping becomes\n"
"$t\\,(T_{m(j,\\sigma),\\,m(j+1,\\sigma)} + T_{m(j+1,\\sigma),\\,m(j,\\sigma)})$ between neighbors with the same spin, and the on-site term is\n"
"$\\tfrac{U}{8} V_{m(j,\\uparrow)} V_{m(j,\\downarrow)}$. The following code builds these terms and prints them, one flow set\n"
"at a time, for $L = 2$.\n"
msgstr ""
"Jika $m(j, \\sigma)$ ialah mod bagi tapak $j$ dan spin $\\sigma$, lompatan menjadi\n"
"$t\\,(T_{m(j,\\sigma),\\,m(j+1,\\sigma)} + T_{m(j+1,\\sigma),\\,m(j,\\sigma)})$ antara jiran dengan spin yang sama, dan sebutan dalam-tapak ialah\n"
"$\\tfrac{U}{8} V_{m(j,\\uparrow)} V_{m(j,\\downarrow)}$. Kod berikut membina sebutan ini dan mencetaknya, satu set aliran\n"
"setiap kali, untuk $L = 2$.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**At the fermionic level, the choice of ordering is only a naming convention.** Blocked and interleaved order give each fermionic mode\n"
"a different index, and nothing else changes. The Hamiltonian is the same operator, with its modes renamed. You can verify this\n"
"with `relabel_modes`, which renames mode $i$ to `permutation[i]` in every term of a `TransferVertexOperator`.\n"
"Anticommutation has no effect, because the operation renames the labels of the modes and does not move particles past each other.\n"
msgstr ""
"**Pada peringkat fermion, pilihan susunan hanyalah konvensyen penamaan.** Susunan berblok dan berselang-seli memberikan setiap mod fermion\n"
"indeks yang berbeza, dan tiada apa-apa lagi yang berubah. Hamiltonian ialah operator yang sama, dengan modnya dinamakan semula. Anda boleh mengesahkannya\n"
"dengan `relabel_modes`, yang menamakan semula mod $i$ kepada `permutation[i]` dalam setiap sebutan `TransferVertexOperator`.\n"
"Penganti-kalisan tidak memberi kesan, kerana operasi ini menamakan semula label mod dan tidak menggerakkan zarah melepasi satu sama lain.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Consider the permutation that takes each blocked index to the interleaved index of the same (site, spin) pair. If this permutation,\n"
"applied to the blocked Hamiltonian, gives the interleaved Hamiltonian, then the two orderings are the same model, and they have the same spectrum\n"
"and Trotter error. A difference can appear only *after* an encoding, where the index decides which qubits are neighbors.\n"
msgstr ""
"Pertimbangkan permutasi yang menukar setiap indeks berblok kepada indeks berselang-seli bagi pasangan (tapak, spin) yang sama. Jika permutasi ini,\n"
"yang dikenakan pada Hamiltonian berblok, memberikan Hamiltonian berselang-seli, maka kedua-dua susunan ialah model yang sama, dan mempunyai spektrum\n"
"dan ralat Trotter yang sama. Perbezaan hanya boleh muncul *selepas* pengekodan, di mana indeks menentukan qubit mana yang berjiran.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Construct the time-evolution circuit {#construct-the-time-evolution-circuit}"
msgstr "Bina circuit evolusi masa {#construct-the-time-evolution-circuit}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Use the Hamiltonian to construct its time evolution as a **fermionic circuit**.\n"
"A `FermionicCircuit` has one wire per fermionic mode, not per qubit, and a single `Evolution` gate holds the whole Hamiltonian.\n"
"The following code builds the circuit for $L = 2$ (four modes, which is small enough to read), before any encoding or qubits are involved.\n"
msgstr ""
"Gunakan Hamiltonian untuk membina evolusi masanya sebagai **circuit fermion**.\n"
"`FermionicCircuit` mempunyai satu wayar bagi setiap mod fermion, bukan bagi setiap qubit, dan satu gate `Evolution` memegang keseluruhan Hamiltonian.\n"
"Kod berikut membina circuit untuk $L = 2$ (empat mod, cukup kecil untuk dibaca), sebelum sebarang pengekodan atau qubit terlibat.\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/spinful-fermi-hubbard-dynamics/extracted-outputs/c81043f3-0.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/spinful-fermi-hubbard-dynamics/extracted-outputs/c81043f3-0.avif)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The `FermionicLieTrotter` synthesis splits that gate by the groups that `flow_set_groups` sets, into one `Evolution` gate per flow\n"
"set. A single call to `decompose()` shows the split. At this small size, the two orderings look alike, because every term acts on two\n"
"modes, and the only difference is *which* two modes.\n"
msgstr ""
"Sintesis `FermionicLieTrotter` memecahkan gate itu mengikut kumpulan yang ditetapkan oleh `flow_set_groups`, kepada satu gate `Evolution` bagi setiap set\n"
"aliran. Satu panggilan `decompose()` menunjukkan pemecahan itu. Pada saiz kecil ini, kedua-dua susunan kelihatan serupa, kerana setiap sebutan bertindak pada dua\n"
"mod, dan satu-satunya perbezaan ialah *dua mod yang mana*.\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/spinful-fermi-hubbard-dynamics/extracted-outputs/292dc410-0.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/spinful-fermi-hubbard-dynamics/extracted-outputs/292dc410-0.avif)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Validate the time-evolution circuit {#validate-the-time-evolution-circuit}"
msgstr "Sahkan circuit evolusi masa {#validate-the-time-evolution-circuit}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Before you continue, compare the results with an independent implementation.\n"
"The `fermi_hubbard_1d` function of ffsim uses $-t\\sum(\\dots) + U' \\sum n_\\uparrow n_\\downarrow - \\mu \\sum n$. This Hamiltonian equals the\n"
"Hamiltonian of this tutorial for $U' = U/2$ and $\\mu = U/4$, up to the constant $UL/8$. Therefore, the lowest eigenvalue at half filling must be the same.\n"
msgstr ""
"Sebelum anda meneruskan, bandingkan keputusan dengan pelaksanaan bebas.\n"
"Fungsi `fermi_hubbard_1d` bagi ffsim menggunakan $-t\\sum(\\dots) + U' \\sum n_\\uparrow n_\\downarrow - \\mu \\sum n$. Hamiltonian ini sama dengan\n"
"Hamiltonian tutorial ini untuk $U' = U/2$ dan $\\mu = U/4$, sehingga pemalar $UL/8$. Oleh itu, nilai eigen terendah pada separuh pengisian mestilah sama.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The same cell also checks the circuit itself. `FermionicCircuit` implements the `apply_unitary` protocol of ffsim, so ffsim can apply the\n"
"time-evolution circuit to a state vector directly. The code compares the result with the matrix exponential of the Hamiltonian, applied to\n"
"the same random state in the half-filling sector.\n"
msgstr ""
"Sel yang sama juga menyemak circuit itu sendiri. `FermionicCircuit` melaksanakan protokol `apply_unitary` ffsim, jadi ffsim boleh mengenakan\n"
"circuit evolusi masa pada vektor keadaan secara langsung. Kod membandingkan keputusan dengan eksponen matriks Hamiltonian, yang dikenakan pada\n"
"keadaan rawak yang sama dalam sektor separuh pengisian.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "3. Encoding the fermions in qubits {#3-encoding-the-fermions-in-qubits}"
msgstr "3. Mengekod fermion dalam qubit {#3-encoding-the-fermions-in-qubits}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The choice of spin ordering starts to matter when an encoding maps the modes to qubits, because the mode index then decides which qubits are neighbors.\n"
"To see this effect, use the same one-ancilla flow-set encoding that section 1 uses for the spinless case.\n"
msgstr ""
"Pilihan susunan spin mula penting apabila pengekodan memetakan mod kepada qubit, kerana indeks mod kemudian menentukan qubit mana yang berjiran.\n"
"Untuk melihat kesan ini, gunakan pengekodan set-aliran satu-ancilla yang sama yang digunakan oleh bahagian 1 untuk kes tanpa spin.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The effect appears as a Pauli pattern, which is a Pauli string together with the offsets of the qubits that it acts on. For example, `ZZ @ (0, 2)` is a Z on some qubit\n"
"$q$ and a Z on qubit $q+2$. The following table prints the patterns for each flow set. The patterns describe only the encoding register, not a\n"
"QPU. The layout decides how far apart two qubits are on a device.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kesan ini muncul sebagai corak Pauli, iaitu rentetan Pauli bersama ofset qubit yang dikenakannya. Sebagai contoh, `ZZ @ (0, 2)` ialah Z pada sesuatu qubit\n"
"$q$ dan Z pada qubit $q+2$. Jadual berikut mencetak corak bagi setiap set aliran. Corak hanya menerangkan daftar pengekodan, bukan\n"
"QPU. Susun atur menentukan sejauh mana dua qubit terpisah pada peranti.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The east (`0`) and west (`1`) flow sets of the *blocked* ordering are the same as in the spinless case, because the hopping terms still act on nearest neighbors.\n"
"The on-site interaction terms, however, become weight-4 and scale with the length $L$ of the chain, as the pattern `ZZZZ @ (0, 1, L, L + 1)` shows.\n"
msgstr ""
"Set aliran timur (`0`) dan barat (`1`) bagi susunan *berblok* sama seperti dalam kes tanpa spin, kerana sebutan lompatan masih bertindak pada jiran terdekat.\n"
"Sebutan interaksi dalam-tapak, walau bagaimanapun, menjadi berat-4 dan berskala dengan panjang $L$ rantai, seperti ditunjukkan oleh corak `ZZZZ @ (0, 1, L, L + 1)`.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In contrast, in the interleaved ordering, none of the encoded flow sets scale with the size of the system.\n"
"The on-site interaction terms remain weight-2 and are identical to the spinless case, because they act on nearest neighbors. The cost is more expensive hopping terms (`YY` and `ZXXZ`).\n"
msgstr ""
"Sebaliknya, dalam susunan berselang-seli, tiada satu pun set aliran terkod yang berskala dengan saiz sistem.\n"
"Sebutan interaksi dalam-tapak kekal berat-2 dan sama dengan kes tanpa spin, kerana ia bertindak pada jiran terdekat. Kosnya ialah sebutan lompatan yang lebih mahal (`YY` dan `ZXXZ`).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The Pauli strings alone do not decide which ordering is cheaper in practice. The answer depends on\n"
"**which qubits the hardware can place next to each other**, and that connectivity is not necessarily one-dimensional.\n"
"A QPU can place the two chains of blocked order side by side, which a single line cannot do. Section 5 uses this property.\n"
msgstr ""
"Rentetan Pauli sahaja tidak menentukan susunan mana yang lebih murah dalam amalan. Jawapannya bergantung pada\n"
"**qubit mana yang boleh diletakkan bersebelahan oleh perkakasan**, dan kesambungan itu belum tentu satu dimensi.\n"
"QPU boleh meletakkan dua rantai susunan berblok bersebelahan, yang tidak boleh dilakukan oleh satu garisan. Bahagian 5 menggunakan sifat ini.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Transpile the `FermionicCircuit` {#transpile-the-fermioniccircuit}"
msgstr "Transpile `FermionicCircuit` {#transpile-the-fermioniccircuit}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"As shown previously, a single Trotter step is one `Evolution` gate that `FermionicLieTrotter` splits into one gate per flow set.\n"
"The `product_formula` argument of `MapperFnEvolutionSynthesis` then decides how each flow set becomes qubit gates.\n"
"This tutorial compares two synthesis paths:\n"
msgstr ""
"Seperti yang ditunjukkan sebelum ini, satu langkah Trotter ialah satu gate `Evolution` yang dipecahkan oleh `FermionicLieTrotter` kepada satu gate bagi setiap set aliran.\n"
"Argumen `product_formula` bagi `MapperFnEvolutionSynthesis` kemudian menentukan cara setiap set aliran menjadi gate qubit.\n"
"Tutorial ini membandingkan dua laluan sintesis:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "The Qiskit `LieTrotter` synthesis, which synthesizes every Pauli rotation separately, in the order that it receives them.\n"
msgstr "Sintesis `LieTrotter` Qiskit, yang mensintesis setiap putaran Pauli secara berasingan, mengikut susunan ia menerimanya.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"A custom `FlowSetSynthesis` class (defined in the following cell) that uses the structure of the flow sets. It recognizes every Pauli shape that the\n"
"encodings in this tutorial produce (`X`, `ZXZ`, `YY`, `ZXXZ`, `ZZ`, and, for two chains, the `ZZZZ` plaquettes), and\n"
"diagonalizes each flow set with a single Clifford layer. For these Hamiltonians, it does not need a term-by-term fallback,\n"
"and the code asserts that every term matches a known shape.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kelas `FlowSetSynthesis` tersuai (ditakrifkan dalam sel berikut) yang menggunakan struktur set aliran. Ia mengenali setiap bentuk Pauli yang dihasilkan oleh\n"
"pengekodan dalam tutorial ini (`X`, `ZXZ`, `YY`, `ZXXZ`, `ZZ`, dan, untuk dua rantai, plakut `ZZZZ`), dan\n"
"mendiagonalkan setiap set aliran dengan satu lapisan Clifford. Untuk Hamiltonian ini, ia tidak memerlukan sandaran sebutan demi sebutan,\n"
"dan kod menegaskan bahawa setiap sebutan sepadan dengan bentuk yang diketahui.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition type=\"note\">\n"
"Work is in progress on an implementation that can find a low-depth diagonalizing Clifford circuit automatically.\n"
"Future releases of `qiskit-fermions` plan to support this feature, which can greatly simplify the use of flow-set-based fermion-to-qubit encodings.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
"The following helper function constructs the transpiler pipeline and applies it to the `FermionicCircuit`.\n"
"The function is useful in this tutorial because the flow-set encoding requires a `CustomF2QLayout`, which couples the transpiler pipeline to the fermionic circuit.\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition type=\"note\">\n"
"Kerja sedang dijalankan ke atas pelaksanaan yang boleh mencari circuit Clifford pendiagonal berkedalaman rendah secara automatik.\n"
"Versi akan datang `qiskit-fermions` dirancang untuk menyokong ciri ini, yang boleh memudahkan sangat penggunaan pengekodan fermion-ke-qubit berasaskan set aliran.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
"Fungsi pembantu berikut membina saluran paip transpiler dan mengenakannya pada `FermionicCircuit`.\n"
"Fungsi ini berguna dalam tutorial ini kerana pengekodan set-aliran memerlukan `CustomF2QLayout`, yang menggandingkan saluran paip transpiler dengan circuit fermion.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "4. Scaling of the interleaved mode ordering {#4-scaling-of-the-interleaved-mode-ordering}"
msgstr "4. Penskalaan susunan mod berselang-seli {#4-scaling-of-the-interleaved-mode-ordering}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Start with the interleaved ordering and the encoding of section 3. With the one ancilla, there are $2L + 1$ qubits in a row. The\n"
"flow sets are `YY @ (0, 1)`, `ZXXZ @ (0, 1, 2, 3)`, and `ZZ @ (0, 2)`, and `FlowSetSynthesis` has a one-Clifford recipe for\n"
"each one. Build the circuit for $L = 4$ (`L_SMALL`, the size of every explicit check), and compare it with\n"
"`LieTrotter` before you measure anything.\n"
msgstr ""
"Mulakan dengan susunan berselang-seli dan pengekodan bahagian 3. Dengan satu ancilla, terdapat $2L + 1$ qubit dalam satu baris. Set\n"
"aliran ialah `YY @ (0, 1)`, `ZXXZ @ (0, 1, 2, 3)`, dan `ZZ @ (0, 2)`, dan `FlowSetSynthesis` mempunyai resipi satu-Clifford bagi\n"
"setiap satu. Bina circuit untuk $L = 4$ (`L_SMALL`, saiz bagi setiap semakan eksplisit), dan bandingkan dengan\n"
"`LieTrotter` sebelum anda mengukur apa-apa.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The previous check shows that the two circuits give identical results, up to a global phase.\n"
"The following drawing shows the regular structure that the flow-set encoding produces in the qubit circuit.\n"
"Later sections show how this structure helps you scale to larger systems.\n"
msgstr ""
"Semakan sebelumnya menunjukkan bahawa kedua-dua circuit memberikan keputusan yang sama, sehingga fasa global.\n"
"Lukisan berikut menunjukkan struktur sekata yang dihasilkan oleh pengekodan set-aliran dalam circuit qubit.\n"
"Bahagian kemudian menunjukkan bagaimana struktur ini membantu anda berskala kepada sistem yang lebih besar.\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/spinful-fermi-hubbard-dynamics/extracted-outputs/67a517b7-0.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/spinful-fermi-hubbard-dynamics/extracted-outputs/67a517b7-0.avif)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Why the circuit needs routing {#why-the-circuit-needs-routing}"
msgstr "Mengapa circuit memerlukan penghalaan {#why-the-circuit-needs-routing}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Every gate of this circuit acts on qubits that are neighbors along the encoding chain, except the gates of the `ZZ` flow set.\n"
"That flow set couples qubits that are two apart (`ZZ @ (0, 2)`, as shown in the table in section 3). On hardware that couples only neighbors, such a pair needs a\n"
"SWAP gate, and the router must insert it. The weakest connectivity that you can use is a plain line of $2L + 1$ qubits. The following code\n"
"counts how many two-qubit gates act on a pair that the line does not couple, for both the term-by-term `LieTrotter` circuit and\n"
"the flow-set circuit.\n"
msgstr ""
"Setiap gate circuit ini bertindak pada qubit yang berjiran di sepanjang rantai pengekodan, kecuali gate set aliran `ZZ`.\n"
"Set aliran itu menggandingkan qubit yang berjarak dua (`ZZ @ (0, 2)`, seperti ditunjukkan dalam jadual di bahagian 3). Pada perkakasan yang hanya menggandingkan jiran, pasangan sedemikian memerlukan\n"
"gate SWAP, dan penghala mesti menyisipkannya. Kesambungan paling lemah yang boleh anda gunakan ialah garisan biasa $2L + 1$ qubit. Kod berikut\n"
"mengira berapa banyak gate dua-qubit bertindak pada pasangan yang tidak digandingkan oleh garisan, bagi circuit `LieTrotter` sebutan demi sebutan dan\n"
"circuit set aliran.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The number of gates that are not on a coupler of the line is the same for both circuits: $2L$ at every size (8 at\n"
"$L = 4$, 100 at $L = 50$). These gates come from the `ZZ @ (0, 2)` pairs. There are $L$ of these pairs, and each one becomes two entangling\n"
"gates. `LieTrotter` already produces a diagonal `ZZ` rotation as a single `rzz` gate, as the flow-set synthesis does, so\n"
"both circuits contain the same $L$ distance-two `rzz` gates. The circuits differ in their total number of gates (884 for\n"
"`LieTrotter` compared with 692 for the flow set at $L = 50$). Therefore, the share of gates that are not on a coupler is 11% compared with 14% at $L = 50$.\n"
msgstr ""
"Bilangan gate yang tidak berada pada gandingan garisan adalah sama untuk kedua-dua circuit: $2L$ pada setiap saiz (8 pada\n"
"$L = 4$, 100 pada $L = 50$). Gate ini datang daripada pasangan `ZZ @ (0, 2)`. Terdapat $L$ pasangan sedemikian, dan setiap satu menjadi dua gate\n"
"penjerat. `LieTrotter` sudah menghasilkan putaran `ZZ` pepenjuru sebagai satu gate `rzz`, seperti sintesis set aliran, jadi\n"
"kedua-dua circuit mengandungi $L$ gate `rzz` jarak-dua yang sama. Circuit berbeza dalam jumlah bilangan gate (884 bagi\n"
"`LieTrotter` berbanding 692 bagi set aliran pada $L = 50$). Oleh itu, bahagian gate yang tidak berada pada gandingan ialah 11% berbanding 14% pada $L = 50$.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The routing problem is the same for both circuits. The synthesis changes the rest of the circuit: the hopping terms (`YY` and\n"
"`ZXXZ`). `LieTrotter` synthesizes these terms one by one, and the flow-set synthesis uses one Clifford circuit for the whole flow set.\n"
msgstr ""
"Masalah penghalaan adalah sama untuk kedua-dua circuit. Sintesis mengubah bahagian circuit yang lain: sebutan lompatan (`YY` dan\n"
"`ZXXZ`). `LieTrotter` mensintesis sebutan ini satu demi satu, dan sintesis set aliran menggunakan satu circuit Clifford untuk keseluruhan set aliran.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Find a chain on a QPU {#find-a-chain-on-a-qpu}"
msgstr "Cari rantai pada QPU {#find-a-chain-on-a-qpu}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"To route onto a QPU, pick a chain of $2L + 1$ qubits on it. The routing task is then the same as on a line. The chain links are couplers, the `ZZ`\n"
"pairs are two apart along the chain, and the layout decides only which physical qubits the chain uses.\n"
msgstr ""
"Untuk menghalakan ke QPU, pilih rantai $2L + 1$ qubit padanya. Tugas penghalaan kemudian sama seperti pada garisan. Pautan rantai ialah gandingan, pasangan `ZZ`\n"
"berjarak dua di sepanjang rantai, dan susun atur hanya menentukan qubit fizikal mana yang digunakan oleh rantai.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The tutorial uses fake backends for two QPUs, so the comparison is of structure, not noise:\n"
msgstr "Tutorial ini menggunakan backend palsu bagi dua QPU, jadi perbandingan adalah mengenai struktur, bukan hingar:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Heron** (`FakeFez`): 156 qubits on a heavy-hex lattice. The lattice has no 4-cycles, but it does contain long simple paths.\n"
msgstr "**Heron** (`FakeFez`): 156 qubit pada kekisi heavy-hex. Kekisi tidak mempunyai kitaran-4, tetapi ia mengandungi laluan ringkas yang panjang.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Nighthawk** (`FakeNighthawk`): 120 qubits on a square lattice of 12 rows and 10 columns. A snake through the rows is a path.\n"
msgstr "**Nighthawk** (`FakeNighthawk`): 120 qubit pada kekisi segi empat sama 12 baris dan 10 lajur. Ular melalui baris ialah satu laluan.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The `find_path` function searches for a path of a given length on any coupling map. It uses a depth-first search, and always prefers the qubit with the fewest\n"
"free neighbors. The `nighthawk_snake` function walks the rows of Nighthawk.\n"
msgstr ""
"Fungsi `find_path` mencari laluan dengan panjang tertentu pada mana-mana peta gandingan. Ia menggunakan carian dalam-dahulu, dan sentiasa mengutamakan qubit dengan jiran\n"
"bebas paling sedikit. Fungsi `nighthawk_snake` menyusuri baris Nighthawk.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The following drawing shows the chains that the two functions return for $L = 50$ (101 qubits), the largest size in this tutorial. Each QPU is\n"
"drawn in full. The gray lines are its couplers, and the light gray circles are the qubits that the circuit does not use. Each colored\n"
"circle is a virtual qubit of the encoded circuit and shows its number. Dark blue circles are spin up (even numbers), light blue circles are\n"
"spin down (odd numbers), and the green circle is the ancilla (the last qubit, $2L$). The dark lines are the chain links between\n"
"consecutive virtual qubits, and they all lie on couplers.\n"
msgstr ""
"Lukisan berikut menunjukkan rantai yang dikembalikan oleh kedua-dua fungsi untuk $L = 50$ (101 qubit), saiz terbesar dalam tutorial ini. Setiap QPU\n"
"dilukis sepenuhnya. Garisan kelabu ialah gandingannya, dan bulatan kelabu muda ialah qubit yang tidak digunakan oleh circuit. Setiap bulatan\n"
"berwarna ialah qubit maya circuit terkod dan menunjukkan nombornya. Bulatan biru tua ialah spin-atas (nombor genap), bulatan biru muda ialah\n"
"spin-bawah (nombor ganjil), dan bulatan hijau ialah ancilla (qubit terakhir, $2L$). Garisan gelap ialah pautan rantai antara\n"
"qubit maya berturutan, dan kesemuanya terletak pada gandingan.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"On Nighthawk, the chain follows the rows of the square lattice in a snake pattern\n"
"and fills ten of its twelve rows. A shorter chain is the beginning of the same snake. On Heron, the chain winds through the\n"
"heavy-hex lattice, and the search finds a different path for every length.\n"
msgstr ""
"Pada Nighthawk, rantai mengikut baris kekisi segi empat sama dalam corak ular\n"
"dan memenuhi sepuluh daripada dua belas barisnya. Rantai yang lebih pendek ialah permulaan ular yang sama. Pada Heron, rantai berliku melalui\n"
"kekisi heavy-hex, dan carian mendapati laluan yang berbeza bagi setiap panjang.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition type=\"note\">\n"
"The longest 1D chain that you can find on a Heron QPU is 127 qubits long, which allows 63 spinful sites in this case study.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition type=\"note\">\n"
"Rantai 1D terpanjang yang boleh anda temui pada QPU Heron ialah 127 qubit panjang, yang membolehkan 63 tapak berspin dalam kajian kes ini.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"When you transpile for real hardware, take the actual noise and calibration data into account to find the\n"
"best layout on the QPU.\n"
msgstr ""
"Apabila anda melakukan transpile untuk perkakasan sebenar, ambil kira data hingar dan kalibrasi sebenar untuk mencari\n"
"susun atur terbaik pada QPU.\n"

