# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Routing and the role of the seeds {#routing-and-the-role-of-the-seeds}"
msgstr "Penghalaan dan peranan seed {#routing-and-the-role-of-the-seeds}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The metrics for routing are the **two-qubit depth** and the **two-qubit gate count** after the preset pass manager at\n"
"optimization level 3, in a given basis. The default basis in this tutorial is `{cz, rz, sx, x}`.\n"
msgstr ""
"Metrik untuk penghalaan ialah **kedalaman dua-qubit** dan **bilangan gate dua-qubit** selepas pengurus laluan pratetap pada\n"
"tahap pengoptimuman 3, dalam asas tertentu. Asas lalai dalam tutorial ini ialah `{cz, rz, sx, x}`.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"*Which part is random?* The layout is fixed, but the router is not deterministic across seeds. The Qiskit `SabreSwap` pass runs\n"
"several randomized trials (20 at optimization level 3), seeded from the `seed_transpiler` value that you pass, and keeps the trial with\n"
"the fewest SWAP gates. Therefore, a seed fixes the whole set of trials, and a different seed gives a different set. The router has\n"
"work to do on every layout, because of the `ZZ` pairs that the previous section counted. Different seeds find different SWAP gates, and the\n"
"router selects by SWAP count, not by two-qubit depth. For these reasons, the code routes every circuit with 20 seeds and **keeps the best result**: the\n"
"smallest two-qubit depth, with ties going to the smaller gate count. The gate count that this tutorial reports is the count of that same circuit.\n"
msgstr ""
"*Bahagian mana yang rawak?* Susun atur ditetapkan, tetapi penghala tidak deterministik merentas seed. Pas `SabreSwap` Qiskit menjalankan\n"
"beberapa percubaan rawak (20 pada tahap pengoptimuman 3), disemai daripada nilai `seed_transpiler` yang anda hantar, dan mengekalkan percubaan dengan\n"
"gate SWAP paling sedikit. Oleh itu, seed menetapkan keseluruhan set percubaan, dan seed yang berbeza memberikan set yang berbeza. Penghala\n"
"ada kerja untuk dilakukan pada setiap susun atur, kerana pasangan `ZZ` yang dikira dalam bahagian sebelumnya. Seed berbeza menemui gate SWAP berbeza, dan\n"
"penghala memilih mengikut bilangan SWAP, bukan kedalaman dua-qubit. Atas sebab ini, kod menghalakan setiap circuit dengan 20 seed dan **mengekalkan keputusan terbaik**: kedalaman\n"
"dua-qubit terkecil, dengan seri diberikan kepada bilangan gate yang lebih kecil. Bilangan gate yang dilaporkan oleh tutorial ini ialah bilangan bagi circuit yang sama itu.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Fractional gates: a second gate set {#fractional-gates-a-second-gate-set}"
msgstr "Gate pecahan: set gate kedua {#fractional-gates-a-second-gate-set}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"IBM Heron and Nighthawk devices can run `rzz(theta)` for $0 < \\theta \\le \\pi/2$ and `rx(theta)` for any $\\theta$ as native\n"
"gates. These *fractional gates* are experimental and are off by default. On a real backend, you turn them on with\n"
"`QiskitRuntimeService.backend(\"ibm_torino\", use_fractional_gates=True)`. This setting is a *backend* option, not a transpiler flag.\n"
"The returned `Target` contains `rzz` with `angle_bounds=[(0, pi/2)]`, and `rx`, and the transpiler then uses them.\n"
msgstr ""
"Peranti IBM Heron dan Nighthawk boleh menjalankan `rzz(theta)` untuk $0 < \\theta \\le \\pi/2$ dan `rx(theta)` untuk sebarang $\\theta$ sebagai gate\n"
"asli. *Gate pecahan* ini bersifat eksperimen dan dimatikan secara lalai. Pada backend sebenar, anda menghidupkannya dengan\n"
"`QiskitRuntimeService.backend(\"ibm_torino\", use_fractional_gates=True)`. Tetapan ini ialah pilihan *backend*, bukan bendera transpiler.\n"
"`Target` yang dikembalikan mengandungi `rzz` dengan `angle_bounds=[(0, pi/2)]`, dan `rx`, dan transpiler kemudian menggunakannya.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The code routes every circuit on the QPUs twice: onto the plain `{cz, rz, sx, x}` default basis, and\n"
"onto a fractional target. A two-qubit layer is a layer of `cz` **or** `rzz` gates, and each of these gates counts as one two-qubit gate.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kod ini menghalakan setiap litar pada QPU sebanyak dua kali: ke atas asas lalai biasa `{cz, rz, sx, x}`, dan\n"
"ke atas sasaran pecahan. Satu lapisan dua-qubit ialah lapisan get `cz` **atau** `rzz`, dan setiap get ini dikira sebagai satu get dua-qubit.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`FakeFez` and `FakeNighthawk` in this environment do not include fractional gates, so the next cell **builds the targets manually**,\n"
"based on the assumptions that are documented in the cell. The depths that later cells report therefore show what the transpiler can do with\n"
"such a gate set. They do not show what a real backend with fractional gates delivers.\n"
msgstr ""
"`FakeFez` dan `FakeNighthawk` dalam persekitaran ini tidak termasuk get pecahan, jadi sel seterusnya **membina sasaran secara manual**,\n"
"berdasarkan andaian yang didokumenkan dalam sel tersebut. Oleh itu, kedalaman yang dilaporkan oleh sel-sel kemudian menunjukkan apa yang boleh dilakukan oleh Transpiler dengan\n"
"set get sedemikian. Kedalaman itu tidak menunjukkan apa yang diberikan oleh Backend sebenar yang mempunyai get pecahan.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Route onto the QPUs, in both gate sets {#route-onto-the-qpus-in-both-gate-sets}"
msgstr "Halakan ke atas QPU, dalam kedua-dua set get {#route-onto-the-qpus-in-both-gate-sets}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The following code routes the flow-set circuit onto Heron and onto Nighthawk with the chains from the previous section. For comparison, it also routes the `LieTrotter` circuit and the flow-set circuit onto a plain line.\n"
msgstr "Kod berikut menghalakan litar set aliran ke atas Heron dan ke atas Nighthawk dengan rantai daripada bahagian sebelumnya. Sebagai perbandingan, kod ini turut menghalakan litar `LieTrotter` dan litar set aliran ke atas garisan biasa.\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/spinful-fermi-hubbard-dynamics/extracted-outputs/47dd8196-0.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/spinful-fermi-hubbard-dynamics/extracted-outputs/47dd8196-0.avif)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Solid lines are the `{cz, rz, sx, x}` basis, and dashed lines are the fractional gate set. The two gray lines are the plain line.\n"
msgstr "Garisan padat ialah asas `{cz, rz, sx, x}`, dan garisan putus-putus ialah set get pecahan. Dua garisan kelabu ialah garisan biasa.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**The synthesis.** With `LieTrotter`, the depth grows with every site (from 47 at $L = 4$ to 599 at $L = 50$, or 12 layers per site).\n"
"The flow-set synthesis stays between 20 and 25 over the same range. The bands reach from the best to the worst of the 20 seeds.\n"
"The gate count grows linearly for both syntheses, and is lower for the flow-set synthesis (882 compared with 1032 at $L = 50$). Therefore, the lower\n"
"depth does not cost extra gates.\n"
msgstr ""
"**Sintesis.** Dengan `LieTrotter`, kedalaman meningkat bagi setiap tapak (daripada 47 pada $L = 4$ kepada 599 pada $L = 50$, atau 12 lapisan bagi setiap tapak).\n"
"Sintesis set aliran kekal antara 20 dan 25 dalam julat yang sama. Jalur ini merangkumi daripada yang terbaik hingga yang terburuk bagi 20 seed.\n"
"Bilangan get meningkat secara linear bagi kedua-dua sintesis, dan lebih rendah bagi sintesis set aliran (882 berbanding 1032 pada $L = 50$). Oleh itu, kedalaman\n"
"yang lebih rendah tidak memerlukan get tambahan.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**The QPUs.** On both QPUs, the flow-set circuit has the same low depth as on the line. The best depth is between 20 and 25 for $L$\n"
"from 4 to 50 on Heron, on Nighthawk, and on the line. The gate counts are also similar. At $L = 10$, the circuit has 164 two-qubit gates on\n"
"Heron, 162 on Nighthawk, and 164 on the line. At $L = 50$, it has 880, 838, and 882. Therefore, **any hardware that has a long\n"
"enough path can run this circuit at an almost constant depth**. The layout is a simple search on Heron, or a snake through\n"
"the rows on Nighthawk.\n"
msgstr ""
"**QPU.** Pada kedua-dua QPU, litar set aliran mempunyai kedalaman rendah yang sama seperti pada garisan. Kedalaman terbaik ialah antara 20 dan 25 bagi $L$\n"
"daripada 4 hingga 50 pada Heron, pada Nighthawk, dan pada garisan. Bilangan get juga serupa. Pada $L = 10$, litar ini mempunyai 164 get dua-qubit pada\n"
"Heron, 162 pada Nighthawk, dan 164 pada garisan. Pada $L = 50$, ia mempunyai 880, 838, dan 882. Oleh itu, **mana-mana perkakasan yang mempunyai laluan yang cukup\n"
"panjang boleh menjalankan litar ini pada kedalaman yang hampir malar**. Susun atur ialah carian ringkas pada Heron, atau laluan berliku-liku merentasi\n"
"baris pada Nighthawk.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Fractional gates.** The fractional gate set lowers the best depth by six layers at every size. On Heron, the depth goes from 20, 20, 23, 23,\n"
"23, 25 to 14, 14, 17, 17, 17, 19. On Nighthawk, it goes from 20, 22, 22, 22, 22, 25 to 14, 16, 16, 16, 16, 19 (at $L = 4, 10, 20, 30,\n"
"40, 50$). This result is expected. The `YY` and `ZZ` flow sets consist of `rzz` rotations, which the fractional gate set runs\n"
"as one gate, while the `cz` basis needs two `cz` gates. These rotations cause the constant drop in depth, and a drop in gate count that\n"
"increases with $L$.\n"
msgstr ""
"**Get pecahan.** Set get pecahan merendahkan kedalaman terbaik sebanyak enam lapisan pada setiap saiz. Pada Heron, kedalaman berubah daripada 20, 20, 23, 23,\n"
"23, 25 kepada 14, 14, 17, 17, 17, 19. Pada Nighthawk, ia berubah daripada 20, 22, 22, 22, 22, 25 kepada 14, 16, 16, 16, 16, 19 (pada $L = 4, 10, 20, 30,\n"
"40, 50$). Keputusan ini dijangka. Set aliran `YY` dan `ZZ` terdiri daripada putaran `rzz`, yang dijalankan oleh set get pecahan\n"
"sebagai satu get, manakala asas `cz` memerlukan dua get `cz`. Putaran ini menyebabkan penurunan malar dalam kedalaman, dan penurunan dalam bilangan get yang\n"
"bertambah dengan $L$.\n"

