# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The following drawing shows one of the routed circuits, for $L = 10$ on Heron (the best of the seeds, from the previous results).\n"
"Each wire is labeled `q_i ↦ p`, which means that virtual qubit `i` of the encoded circuit starts on physical qubit `p` of the device.\n"
"For Nighthawk, `p = 10 * row + col`. The drawing shows only the qubits that the circuit acts on.\n"
msgstr ""
"Lukisan berikut menunjukkan salah satu litar yang dihalakan, bagi $L = 10$ pada Heron (seed terbaik, daripada keputusan sebelumnya).\n"
"Setiap wayar dilabel `q_i ↦ p`, yang bermaksud qubit maya `i` bagi litar yang dikodkan bermula pada qubit fizikal `p` peranti tersebut.\n"
"Bagi Nighthawk, `p = 10 * row + col`. Lukisan ini hanya menunjukkan qubit yang dikenakan tindakan oleh litar.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "5. Connectivity of Nighthawk devices {#5-connectivity-of-nighthawk-devices}"
msgstr "5. Kesambungan peranti Nighthawk {#5-connectivity-of-nighthawk-devices}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The interleaved circuit needs only a path. Suppose the QPU offers more connectivity. The qubits of Nighthawk are on a square\n"
"lattice, and a square lattice contains a **ladder**: two parallel chains whose rungs are real couplers. A ladder is the\n"
"interaction graph of the Hubbard model in blocked order. The spin-up chain is on one rail, the spin-down chain is on the other, and the on-site term acts\n"
"across a rung.\n"
msgstr ""
"Litar berselang-seli hanya memerlukan satu laluan. Andaikan QPU menawarkan lebih banyak kesambungan. Qubit Nighthawk berada pada kekisi\n"
"segi empat sama, dan kekisi segi empat sama mengandungi **tangga**: dua rantai selari yang anak tangganya ialah pengganding sebenar. Tangga ialah\n"
"graf interaksi model Hubbard dalam tertib berblok. Rantai spin-atas berada pada satu landasan, rantai spin-bawah berada pada landasan yang lain, dan sebutan di tapak bertindak\n"
"merentasi anak tangga.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The single-chain encoding of section 4 cannot use the ladder. It places all $2L$ modes along **one** chain. With blocked order,\n"
"the spin-up and spin-down blocks are joined end to end, and the on-site plaquettes stretch across the join. Instead, give\n"
"**each spin its own chain and its own ancilla**:\n"
msgstr ""
"Pengekodan rantai tunggal dalam bahagian 4 tidak dapat menggunakan tangga. Ia meletakkan semua $2L$ mod di sepanjang **satu** rantai. Dengan tertib berblok,\n"
"blok spin-atas dan spin-bawah disambung hujung ke hujung, dan plakuet di tapak terbentang merentasi sambungan itu. Sebaliknya, berikan\n"
"**setiap spin rantainya sendiri dan ancilla-nya sendiri**:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Spin-up modes $0..L-1$ are on qubits $0..L-1$, with the ancilla on qubit $L$.\n"
msgstr "Mod spin-atas $0..L-1$ berada pada qubit $0..L-1$, dengan ancilla pada qubit $L$.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Spin-down modes $L..2L-1$ are on qubits $L+1..2L$, with the ancilla on qubit $2L+1$.\n"
msgstr "Mod spin-bawah $L..2L-1$ berada pada qubit $L+1..2L$, dengan ancilla pada qubit $2L+1$.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Each block uses the same images as before: $V_j = Z_qZ_{q+1}$, $T_{j,j+1} = -X_{q+1}/2$, and $T_{j+1,j} = \\tfrac12 Z_qX_{q+1}Z_{q+2}$,\n"
"where $q$ is the qubit of mode $j$. The total is $2L + 2$ qubits, which is one more than before.\n"
msgstr ""
"Setiap blok menggunakan imej yang sama seperti sebelumnya: $V_j = Z_qZ_{q+1}$, $T_{j,j+1} = -X_{q+1}/2$, dan $T_{j+1,j} = \\tfrac12 Z_qX_{q+1}Z_{q+2}$,\n"
"dengan $q$ ialah qubit bagi mod $j$. Jumlahnya ialah $2L + 2$ qubit, iaitu satu lebih banyak daripada sebelumnya.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Every flow set is now local on the ladder. The `X` and `ZXZ` terms act along a rail, and the interaction `ZZZZ @ (0, 1, L+1, L+2)` is a 2x2\n"
"plaquette (two neighbors on one rail and the two qubits next to them on the other rail).\n"
msgstr ""
"Setiap set aliran kini setempat pada tangga. Sebutan `X` dan `ZXZ` bertindak di sepanjang satu landasan, dan interaksi `ZZZZ @ (0, 1, L+1, L+2)` ialah plakuet 2x2\n"
"(dua jiran pada satu landasan dan dua qubit di sebelahnya pada landasan yang lain).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In the encoded space, spin-up and spin-down operators now *commute* instead of anticommuting. This difference has no effect on this\n"
"Hamiltonian, because it contains only bilinears of the same spin and products of vertex operators. An operator with hopping between spins\n"
"raises an error in the action, so it cannot silently give a wrong answer. Perform the same check against\n"
"the known `LieTrotter` circuit as for the single-ancilla interleaved ordering:\n"
msgstr ""
"Dalam ruang yang dikodkan, pengendali spin-atas dan spin-bawah kini *berkalis tukar tertib* dan bukannya antiberkalis tukar tertib. Perbezaan ini tidak memberi kesan kepada\n"
"Hamiltonian ini, kerana ia hanya mengandungi bilinear bagi spin yang sama dan hasil darab pengendali bucu. Pengendali dengan lompatan antara spin\n"
"menimbulkan ralat dalam tindakan, jadi ia tidak boleh secara senyap memberikan jawapan yang salah. Lakukan semakan yang sama terhadap\n"
"litar `LieTrotter` yang diketahui seperti bagi tertib berselang-seli ancilla tunggal:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "A ladder on the QPU {#a-ladder-on-the-qpu}"
msgstr "Tangga pada QPU {#a-ladder-on-the-qpu}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"A chain of $L + 1$ qubits fits on Nighthawk in a straight line if it has at most 12 qubits (along the 12 rows) or at most 10\n"
"(along the 10 columns). Therefore, up to $L = 11$, the two chains are side by side on two neighboring grid lines, rung by rung, and\n"
"every coupler that the circuit needs is a real coupler. The `folded_ladder` function returns this layout. For larger $L$, it also folds the ladder,\n"
"as section 6 describes. The function also selects the orientation that needs fewer strips, and selects the horizontal orientation if both need the same number.\n"
msgstr ""
"Rantai $L + 1$ qubit muat pada Nighthawk dalam garisan lurus jika ia mempunyai paling banyak 12 qubit (di sepanjang 12 baris) atau paling banyak 10\n"
"(di sepanjang 10 lajur). Oleh itu, sehingga $L = 11$, kedua-dua rantai berada bersebelahan pada dua garisan grid yang berjiran, anak tangga demi anak tangga, dan\n"
"setiap pengganding yang diperlukan oleh litar ialah pengganding sebenar. Fungsi `folded_ladder` mengembalikan susun atur ini. Bagi $L$ yang lebih besar, ia turut melipat tangga,\n"
"seperti yang diterangkan dalam bahagian 6. Fungsi ini juga memilih orientasi yang memerlukan lebih sedikit jalur, dan memilih orientasi mendatar jika kedua-duanya memerlukan bilangan yang sama.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The following drawings show both straight cases. For $L = 8$, a chain of 9 qubits fits along the 10 columns, so the ladder is\n"
"horizontal. For $L = 10$, a chain of 11 qubits does not fit along the 10 columns (it needs two strips), but it fits along\n"
"the 12 rows, so the layout uses a vertical ladder.\n"
msgstr ""
"Lukisan berikut menunjukkan kedua-dua kes lurus. Bagi $L = 8$, rantai 9 qubit muat di sepanjang 10 lajur, jadi tangga ini\n"
"mendatar. Bagi $L = 10$, rantai 11 qubit tidak muat di sepanjang 10 lajur (ia memerlukan dua jalur), tetapi ia muat di sepanjang\n"
"12 baris, jadi susun atur ini menggunakan tangga menegak.\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/spinful-fermi-hubbard-dynamics/extracted-outputs/25d1a8f2-0.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/spinful-fermi-hubbard-dynamics/extracted-outputs/25d1a8f2-0.avif)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The following code compares the two orderings at the sizes that fit natively: interleaved on the snake, and blocked on the ladder, both on Nighthawk and in\n"
"both gate sets.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kod berikut membandingkan kedua-dua tertib pada saiz yang muat secara natif: berselang-seli pada laluan berliku-liku, dan berblok pada tangga, kedua-duanya pada Nighthawk dan dalam\n"
"kedua-dua set get.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"For the blocked ladder that fits natively on the QPU ($L \\leq 10$), no gates are off a coupler.\n"
"Therefore, for these sizes, the routing step is not expected to change the circuit statistics.\n"
msgstr ""
"Bagi tangga berblok yang muat secara natif pada QPU ($L \\leq 10$), tiada get yang berada di luar pengganding.\n"
"Oleh itu, bagi saiz ini, langkah penghalaan tidak dijangka mengubah statistik litar.\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/spinful-fermi-hubbard-dynamics/extracted-outputs/b8e745c2-0.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/spinful-fermi-hubbard-dynamics/extracted-outputs/b8e745c2-0.avif)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"At the sizes that fit natively ($L \\le 10$), the blocked circuit is **about half as deep**. At $L = 10$, its depth is 10 compared with 22 in the `cz` basis, and\n"
"8 compared with 16 with fractional gates. At $L = 4$, the values are 10 compared with 20, and 8 compared with 14. The depth of the blocked circuit does not change\n"
"between $L = 4$ and $L = 10$. The blocked circuit also needs fewer gates. At $L = 10$, it needs 82 compared with 162 in the `cz` basis, and 72 compared with 116 with\n"
"fractional gates. These results are expected, because no gates are off a coupler.\n"
"Therefore, one more ancilla qubit reduces the depth by a factor of two for these sizes.\n"
msgstr ""
"Pada saiz yang muat secara natif ($L \\le 10$), litar berblok **kira-kira separuh sedalam**. Pada $L = 10$, kedalamannya ialah 10 berbanding 22 dalam asas `cz`, dan\n"
"8 berbanding 16 dengan get pecahan. Pada $L = 4$, nilainya ialah 10 berbanding 20, dan 8 berbanding 14. Kedalaman litar berblok tidak berubah\n"
"antara $L = 4$ dan $L = 10$. Litar berblok juga memerlukan lebih sedikit get. Pada $L = 10$, ia memerlukan 82 berbanding 162 dalam asas `cz`, dan 72 berbanding 116 dengan\n"
"get pecahan. Keputusan ini dijangka, kerana tiada get yang berada di luar pengganding.\n"
"Oleh itu, satu qubit ancilla tambahan mengurangkan kedalaman dengan faktor dua bagi saiz ini.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"At $L = 12$, this advantage ends. A chain of 13 qubits does not fit on a straight grid line, so the ladder must bend. Then six of the\n"
"98 two-qubit gates are off a coupler, and the depth of the blocked circuit increases to 25 in the `cz` basis and 23 with fractional gates. These depths are\n"
"*greater* than the interleaved depths at the same size (22 and 16). The next section examines that fold.\n"
"As before, you can also view the routed circuit of the blocked encoding for $L = 10$:\n"
msgstr ""
"Pada $L = 12$, kelebihan ini berakhir. Rantai 13 qubit tidak muat pada garisan grid yang lurus, jadi tangga mesti dibengkokkan. Kemudian enam daripada\n"
"98 get dua-qubit berada di luar pengganding, dan kedalaman litar berblok meningkat kepada 25 dalam asas `cz` dan 23 dengan get pecahan. Kedalaman ini\n"
"*lebih besar* daripada kedalaman berselang-seli pada saiz yang sama (22 dan 16). Bahagian seterusnya meneliti lipatan itu.\n"
"Seperti sebelumnya, anda juga boleh melihat litar yang dihalakan bagi pengekodan berblok untuk $L = 10$:\n"

