# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "6. Scaling beyond the native dimensions of Nighthawk {#6-scaling-beyond-the-native-dimensions-of-nighthawk}"
msgstr "6. Penskalaan melangkaui dimensi natif Nighthawk {#6-scaling-beyond-the-native-dimensions-of-nighthawk}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"For $L$ greater than 11, a chain does not fit in a straight line, so the ladder must **fold**. The `folded_ladder` function cuts each chain into segments, and\n"
"stacks the segments in strips of two adjacent grid lines. Each strip starts at the opposite end from the end of the previous strip.\n"
"Each strip boundary stretches one spin-up link and one spin-down link from distance 1 to distance 2, and this stretch is the only imperfection.\n"
"Rungs stay real couplers everywhere. A ladder cannot bend on a square lattice without that stretch, so fewer strips are\n"
"better. The strips can run along the 12 rows instead of the 10 columns, which needs fewer strips, and `folded_ladder` selects\n"
"the orientation that needs fewer strips (the orientation changes between $L=49$ and $L=50$). In the following drawings, the stretched links are red and dotted.\n"
msgstr ""
"Bagi $L$ yang lebih besar daripada 11, rantai tidak muat dalam garisan lurus, jadi tangga mesti **dilipat**. Fungsi `folded_ladder` memotong setiap rantai kepada segmen, dan\n"
"menyusun segmen dalam jalur yang terdiri daripada dua garisan grid bersebelahan. Setiap jalur bermula pada hujung yang bertentangan dengan hujung jalur sebelumnya.\n"
"Setiap sempadan jalur meregangkan satu pautan spin-atas dan satu pautan spin-bawah daripada jarak 1 kepada jarak 2, dan regangan ini ialah satu-satunya kecacatan.\n"
"Anak tangga kekal sebagai pengganding sebenar di mana-mana. Tangga tidak boleh dibengkokkan pada kekisi segi empat sama tanpa regangan itu, jadi lebih sedikit jalur adalah\n"
"lebih baik. Jalur boleh dijalankan di sepanjang 12 baris dan bukannya 10 lajur, yang memerlukan lebih sedikit jalur, dan `folded_ladder` memilih\n"
"orientasi yang memerlukan lebih sedikit jalur (orientasi berubah antara $L=49$ dan $L=50$). Dalam lukisan berikut, pautan yang diregangkan berwarna merah dan bertitik.\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/spinful-fermi-hubbard-dynamics/extracted-outputs/c35f19ce-0.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/spinful-fermi-hubbard-dynamics/extracted-outputs/c35f19ce-0.avif)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The following code shows the cost of the fold. It runs the same comparison as before, up to 50 sites, and adds blocked order on Heron.\n"
"The heavy-hex lattice has no ladder, so on Heron the router chooses the layout. This comparison is the final comparison of all four\n"
"variants, with the depth on the left and the two-qubit gate count on the right.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kod berikut menunjukkan kos lipatan. Ia menjalankan perbandingan yang sama seperti sebelumnya, sehingga 50 tapak, dan menambah tertib berblok pada Heron.\n"
"Kekisi heavy-hex tidak mempunyai tangga, jadi pada Heron penghala memilih susun atur. Perbandingan ini ialah perbandingan akhir bagi keempat-empat\n"
"varian, dengan kedalaman di sebelah kiri dan bilangan get dua-qubit di sebelah kanan.\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/spinful-fermi-hubbard-dynamics/extracted-outputs/9756fef7-0.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/spinful-fermi-hubbard-dynamics/extracted-outputs/9756fef7-0.avif)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Between $L = 10$ and $L = 12$, the depth of the blocked circuit increases from 10 to 25 in the `cz` basis (from eight to 23 with fractional\n"
"gates), and then stays the same up to $L = 50$. **The fold increases the depth once, not once per strip.** The drawing for $L = 50$ has four\n"
"folds and eight stretched links, and the depth is the same as at $L = 12$, which has one fold. The depth stays the same because the\n"
"depth penalties of all folds occur in parallel.\n"
msgstr ""
"Antara $L = 10$ dan $L = 12$, kedalaman litar berblok meningkat daripada 10 kepada 25 dalam asas `cz` (daripada lapan kepada 23 dengan get\n"
"pecahan), dan kemudian kekal sama sehingga $L = 50$. **Lipatan meningkatkan kedalaman sekali sahaja, bukan sekali bagi setiap jalur.** Lukisan bagi $L = 50$ mempunyai empat\n"
"lipatan dan lapan pautan yang diregangkan, dan kedalamannya sama seperti pada $L = 12$, yang mempunyai satu lipatan. Kedalaman kekal sama kerana\n"
"penalti kedalaman bagi semua lipatan berlaku secara selari.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Result of the comparison.** Beyond the width of the QPU, blocked order loses its depth advantage. At $L = 50$, both orderings\n"
"reach 25 in the `cz` basis. The best interleaved seed reaches 22 between $L = 12$ and $L = 40$, but its median is 23 to 25.\n"
"With fractional gates, blocked order (23) is deeper than interleaved order (19). Blocked order still has a lower gate count: 462 compared with 838\n"
"in the `cz` basis (45% fewer) and 412 compared with 592 with fractional gates (30% fewer), at the cost of one more qubit. Fewer gates\n"
"can mean less accumulated error on a real device, which can be a reason to prefer blocked order on a QPU with a ladder. The\n"
"observable that you measure at the end of the circuit can also affect the choice of encoding.\n"
msgstr ""
"**Keputusan perbandingan.** Melangkaui lebar QPU, tertib berblok kehilangan kelebihan kedalamannya. Pada $L = 50$, kedua-dua tertib\n"
"mencapai 25 dalam asas `cz`. Seed berselang-seli terbaik mencapai 22 antara $L = 12$ dan $L = 40$, tetapi mediannya ialah 23 hingga 25.\n"
"Dengan get pecahan, tertib berblok (23) lebih dalam daripada tertib berselang-seli (19). Tertib berblok masih mempunyai bilangan get yang lebih rendah: 462 berbanding 838\n"
"dalam asas `cz` (45% lebih sedikit) dan 412 berbanding 592 dengan get pecahan (30% lebih sedikit), dengan kos satu qubit tambahan. Get yang lebih sedikit\n"
"boleh bermaksud ralat terkumpul yang lebih kecil pada peranti sebenar, yang boleh menjadi sebab untuk memilih tertib berblok pada QPU yang mempunyai tangga. \n"
"Kebolehcerapan yang anda ukur pada penghujung litar juga boleh mempengaruhi pilihan pengekodan.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**On Heron, which has no ladder, blocked order is much worse.** Its best depth grows from 29 at $L = 4$ to 95 at $L = 50$\n"
"in the `cz` basis (92 with fractional gates), and the median and worst seeds at $L = 50$ give 134 and 166.\n"
msgstr ""
"**Pada Heron, yang tidak mempunyai tangga, tertib berblok jauh lebih teruk.** Kedalaman terbaiknya meningkat daripada 29 pada $L = 4$ kepada 95 pada $L = 50$\n"
"dalam asas `cz` (92 dengan get pecahan), dan seed median dan terburuk pada $L = 50$ memberikan 134 dan 166.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "7. Beyond one dimension {#7-beyond-one-dimension}"
msgstr "7. Melangkaui satu dimensi {#7-beyond-one-dimension}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"All of the previous sections are one-dimensional, where the hardware needs to hold only a path or a ladder. A square lattice of sites is\n"
"the case where the square connectivity of Nighthawk matters most, so this section briefly examines it. To keep the section short, it omits spin\n"
"and uses the **spinless** model of the [Simulate 2D Fermi-Hubbard dynamics with flow sets](/addons/qiskit-fermions/guides/2-d-fermi-hubbard) guide\n"
"(Gandon et al., arXiv:2512.11418). That model has hopping and interaction on every nearest-neighbor bond of an $R \\times C$ lattice.\n"
msgstr ""
"Semua bahagian sebelumnya adalah satu dimensi, yang mana perkakasan hanya perlu menampung satu laluan atau tangga. Kekisi tapak segi empat sama ialah\n"
"kes yang paling menunjukkan kepentingan kesambungan segi empat sama Nighthawk, jadi bahagian ini meneliti kes tersebut secara ringkas. Untuk memendekkan bahagian ini, spin diabaikan\n"
"dan model **tanpa spin** daripada panduan [Simulate 2D Fermi-Hubbard dynamics with flow sets](/addons/qiskit-fermions/guides/2-d-fermi-hubbard) digunakan\n"
"(Gandon et al., arXiv:2512.11418). Model itu mempunyai lompatan dan interaksi pada setiap ikatan jiran terdekat bagi kekisi $R \\times C$.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In the Verstraete-Cirac encoding of the model, every site gets **its own ancilla** ($N = RC$ modes use $2N$ qubits), and the hopping splits into **four flow\n"
"sets** (east, west, north, and south). A Clifford circuit of two-qubit depth 2, which acts on all rows or all columns\n"
"at the same time, diagonalizes each flow set. As in 1D, the depth of the circuit therefore does not grow with the lattice. The guide shows each of these steps, but it\n"
"does not transpile to a given connectivity. The following drawing shows how the model fits on Nighthawk.\n"
msgstr ""
"Dalam pengekodan Verstraete-Cirac bagi model ini, setiap tapak mendapat **ancilla-nya sendiri** ($N = RC$ mod menggunakan $2N$ qubit), dan lompatan terbahagi kepada **empat set\n"
"aliran** (timur, barat, utara, dan selatan). Litar Clifford berkedalaman dua-qubit 2, yang bertindak pada semua baris atau semua lajur\n"
"pada masa yang sama, mengpepenjurukan setiap set aliran. Seperti dalam 1D, kedalaman litar oleh itu tidak bertambah dengan kekisi. Panduan tersebut menunjukkan setiap langkah ini, tetapi\n"
"ia tidak mentranspilasi kepada kesambungan tertentu. Lukisan berikut menunjukkan cara model ini muat pada Nighthawk.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**The stripe layout on Nighthawk.** Lattice row $r$ runs down QPU column $r$ as a stripe that alternates site, ancilla, site,\n"
"ancilla (lattice column $c$ is on QPU rows $2c$ and $2c+1$). A site and its own ancilla are neighbors, an ancilla and the *next*\n"
"site along the row are neighbors, and vertical neighbors are on adjacent QPU columns. Therefore, **all hopping terms are on couplers**, and\n"
"the Clifford circuits need no routing. The interaction between two sites of the same row is not native, because the two sites are two QPU qubits\n"
"apart, with the ancilla between them (the red arcs). These pairs are the same $\\texttt{ZZ}$-type pairs that you routed in 1D, with one `rzz` gate per\n"
"horizontal bond, so the routing cost is similar to the cost in 1D. The largest lattice that fits this layout is $10 \\times 6$\n"
"(60 sites, which use all 120 qubits).\n"
msgstr ""
"**Susun atur jalur pada Nighthawk.** Baris kekisi $r$ berjalan menurun lajur QPU $r$ sebagai jalur yang berselang-seli tapak, ancilla, tapak,\n"
"ancilla (lajur kekisi $c$ berada pada baris QPU $2c$ dan $2c+1$). Satu tapak dan ancilla-nya sendiri ialah jiran, satu ancilla dan tapak *seterusnya*\n"
"di sepanjang baris ialah jiran, dan jiran menegak berada pada lajur QPU yang bersebelahan. Oleh itu, **semua sebutan lompatan berada pada pengganding**, dan\n"
"litar Clifford tidak memerlukan penghalaan. Interaksi antara dua tapak pada baris yang sama bukan natif, kerana kedua-dua tapak itu terpisah dua qubit QPU\n"
"dengan ancilla di antaranya (lengkok merah). Pasangan ini ialah pasangan jenis $\\texttt{ZZ}$ yang sama yang anda halakan dalam 1D, dengan satu get `rzz` bagi setiap\n"
"ikatan mendatar, jadi kos penghalaan adalah serupa dengan kos dalam 1D. Kekisi terbesar yang muat pada susun atur ini ialah $10 \\times 6$\n"
"(60 tapak, yang menggunakan kesemua 120 qubit).\n"

